     "type": "text",
     "text": "GET /api/part-sales/{invoiceId}/list-credit-available-parts",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "code"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " returns 500 for a part that has no catalogue entry, and the dialog renders that failure as \"No parts on this invoice are available for credit.\" - so the user is told there is nothing to credit rather than that something went wrong. Reproduced three times (requestIds 91fa4062-e2db-4d74-b653-c14c34c68256, 3197b27f-c077-493b-b60f-ed6cd4499cf2, ec16d0ca-d25d-4d7a-83d7-05b3e37e2d1e). The same endpoint answers 200 for ordinary vendor-sourced parts, so it is an edge case rather than a blocker, and it is unrelated to sales-tax rounding."
    }
